WEBVTT

0
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.859
Sprezzature is an AI engine for Design.
Maps draws on real ground.

1
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:12.440
You hold an export of conflict events.
Every row says how well it is located.

2
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.937
Drop the point layer.
Every row becomes the same confident dot.

3
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.250
The map asserts a street corner the
source never gave, once per row.

4
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.040
3 generators draw here,
on real coastlines and measured relief.

5
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.000
A ramp stretched end to end is a story.
Here the legend names its classes.

6
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:48.960
The world sits on Equal Earth:
ŠAVRIČ, PATTERSON and JENNY, 2018.

7
00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:53.597
Then the plate that draws no map.
The land appears because events fell.

8
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.600
ACLED, the armed conflict location
and event data project, grades 1 to 3.

9
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:05.360
The Uppsala conflict data program,
UCDP, grades it 1 to 7.

10
00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:10.280
So a named place is a filled disc,
and an approximate one a hollow ring.

11
00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:14.760
A province pinned to its capital
gets a broken ring, never a dot.

12
00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.640
That wording is ACLED's own,
read out of its codebook.

13
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:27.240
Ukraine. 6 markers, 6 rings,
because the source said approximate.

14
00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:32.475
Nothing on this plate claims a
position the source never gave.

15
00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:44.640
Go to sprezzature.ai,
and drop a GitHub star if it deserves it.

16
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.199
Make it, audit it, take a look at it.
